    </p>

    <h2 id="billing">14. Paid Plans, Billing and Taxes</h2>
    <p>
      This section applies to paid plans of the cloud-hosted Service. Plan limits and prices are shown on the pricing page and at checkout.
    </p>
    <h3>14.1 Billing and Renewal</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Paid plans are billed in advance, monthly or annually, as you choose at checkout</li>
      <li>Subscriptions renew automatically for the same period until cancelled</li>
      <li>Payments are processed by Stripe Payments Europe, Ltd. (Ireland). We do not store your full card details</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>14.2 Taxes</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Prices exclude VAT and other applicable taxes</li>
      <li>VAT is calculated at checkout based on your location</li>
      <li>Business customers in the EU who provide a valid VAT identification number may be invoiced under the reverse charge mechanism, where applicable</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>14.3 Cancellation</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>You can cancel at any time from the Stripe Customer Portal, linked from your billing settings</li>
      <li>Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period. You keep access to the paid plan until then</li>
      <li>At the end of the paid period, a cancelled account continues on the Free plan (7-day retention)</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>14.4 Downgrade and Data Retention</h3>
    <p>
      When a subscription is cancelled, the account moves to the Free plan, and data older than the Free plan retention (7 days) will be deleted. When you move to another paid plan with shorter retention, data older than the retention of that plan will be deleted. In both cases we notify you by email at least 14 days before that deletion, and you can export your data while your account is active, including during this notice period.
    </p>
    <h3>14.5 Failed Payments</h3>
    <p>
      If a payment fails, we keep your plan active for 7 days while the payment is retried. After that, the account is downgraded to the Free plan and section 14.4 applies.
    </p>
    <h3>14.6 Quotas</h3>
    <p>
      Paid plans include a 10% grace over the monthly quota, with immediate notice. After that, ingestion is paused until the monthly quota resets on the 1st of the next month (UTC) or until you upgrade. Quotas are monthly and reset on the 1st of each calendar month (UTC), regardless of whether you are billed monthly or annually. We do not charge overage fees.
    </p>
    <h3>14.7 Refunds</h3>
    <p>
      Except where the law or section 15 gives you a right to a refund, fees are non-refundable, and we do not refund partial periods after cancellation.
    </p>
    <h3>14.8 Price Changes</h3>
    <p>
      We may change prices with at least 30 days' notice by email. The change applies from your next renewal, and you can cancel before then.
    </p>

    <h2 id="withdrawal">15. Right of Withdrawal for EU Consumers</h2>
