      The Service is available to both businesses and consumers. If you are a consumer in the EU (a person acting outside any trade, business or profession), you have a 14-day right to withdraw from a distance contract without giving a reason, starting from the day the contract is concluded.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Service is digital and starts as soon as you pay. To purchase a paid plan you must expressly confirm the following at checkout, by ticking the box in Stripe Checkout:
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      I agree to the Terms of Service and request that the service starts immediately. I acknowledge that I lose my right of withdrawal once the service has started.
    </blockquote>
    <ul>
      <li>A purchase requires this express request. The service starts at the moment of payment, and the 14-day right of withdrawal is therefore lost once the service has started, as provided by the EU Consumer Rights Directive (2011/83/EU)</li>
      <li>Questions about your purchase can be sent to <a href="mailto:legal@logtide.dev">legal@logtide.dev</a></li>
      <li>This section does not limit any mandatory consumer rights you have under the law of your country</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      [OPERATOR: confirm with counsel the wording on loss of the right of withdrawal for subscription services, any proportional payment for service already used, and whether a model withdrawal form must be provided.]
    </p>

    <h2>16. Contact</h2>
